{"id":"euler-copybot-2023","slug":"euler-copybot-2023","sub":null,"name":"Euler Finance: copied exploit contract executes the DAI-market exploit first, proceeds routed to the hacker by a hard-coded destination","date":"2023-03-13","one_liner":"A fresh EOA copied the Euler attacker's exploit contract one block after its deploy, swapping only the owner address, and ran its DAI-market entry point at block 16817996 position 0: 8,877,507 DAI out of Euler. Funds went to the attacker's hard-coded wallet; the copier captured nothing.","bot":"anon searcher","race_type":"deploy-window-copy","narrative":"Sub-type: copy-of-contract front-run that captured nothing (the copier's own contract paid the hacker). (1) Real attacker = EOA 0xB2698C2D99aD2C302a95A8Db26B08d17A77CEdd4 (funded by Tornado Cash 1 ETH pool) which deployed exploit contract 0x036cec1a... in block 16817993 idx 35 (tx 0x50dc9c91..., 3 gwei tip). (2) One block later (16817994 idx 5, tx 0x725db76c...) a different EOA 0x5F259D0b... deployed a contract whose creation calldata is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the attacker's (17,115 bytes) except 4 occurrences of the 20-byte address 0xB2698C2D... replaced by 0x5F259D0b... (80 differing bytes; incidents/euler-copybot-2023/bytecode_diff.json); the hard-coded 0xb66cd966... (profit/withdraw destination) was left untouched. (3) In block 16817996 idx 0 (tx 0xc310a0af..., 37.9 gwei tip, top of block by gas price) the copier called the DAI-market entry point (0x863df8af) of its copy: Aave flash loan 30M DAI -> Euler exploit -> 38,904,507.35 DAI out of Euler, 30,027,000 DAI repaid, 8,877,507.35 DAI net left in the copy. The hacker never called that entry point on its own contract; its own first attack call (WETH market, tx 0xa476fad7, block 16818013 idx 44) came 17 blocks (~3.5 min) later and failed out-of-gas, first success 0x47ac3527 at 16818024. So the copy beat the hacker to the first exploit tx by 17 blocks and to the DAI market entirely. It captured $0 for the copier: the DAI sat in the copy until the copier itself called withdraw() (0x3ccfd60b) in block 16818823 (tx 0xdae809e4, 11:38:11Z), which sent all 8,877,507.35 DAI to the hard-coded 0xb66cd966... (hacker's cash-out wallet; same wallet received the hacker's own loot from contract 0x036cec1a). Calls to the copy's withdraw/entry points by other addresses all reverted. Caveats: the copier's claim to be an MEV bot rests on its on-chain message (tx 0x44b559c8..., block 16818973); on-chain it is a fresh single-purpose EOA (nonce 0 at the copy, funded 4.22 ETH on 2023-02-12, no prior MEV history). Whether it saw the hacker's deploy tx in the mempool or only after block 16817993 (12 s earlier) is unknowable: in-block evidence only. It is not a calldata replay of a pending attacker call tx; it is a copy of the attacker's deployment plus an adapted call.","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1678697459000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":5989453,"block":{"number":16817996,"hash":"0xde714b65354d54e684a95d80a1da7f668e8b2ee6ae8b5779f69ab9e04468b859","ts_ms":1678697459000,"ntx":155,"builder":"Flashbots","fee_recipient":"0xdafea492d9c6733ae3d56b7ed1adb60692c98bc5","gas_used":20084900,"base_fee_gwei":18.919454698,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_16817996.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_16817996.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_16817996.json","slot":null}},"strip":[[0,1,"bot",37.899,0.0],[1,1,"",17.503,0.0],[2,1,"",0.0,0.0014],[3,1,"",10.766,0.0],[4,1,"",7.348,0.0],[5,1,"",6.281,0.0],[6,1,"",6.0,0.0],[7,1,"",5.789,0.0],[8,1,"",5.081,0.0],[9,1,"",4.829,0.0],[10,1,"",4.081,0.0],[11,1,"",4.081,0.0],[12,1,"",4.081,0.0],[13,0,"",4.081,0.0],[14,0,"",4.081,0.0],[15,0,"",4.081,0.0],[16,1,"",4.081,0.0],[17,1,"",3.839,0.0],[18,1,"",3.243,0.0],[19,1,"",3.0,0.0],[20,1,"",3.0,0.0],[21,1,"",2.653,0.0],[22,1,"",2.5,0.0],[23,1,"",2.5,0.0],[24,1,"",2.3,0.0],[25,1,"",2.25,0.0],[26,1,"",2.25,0.0],[27,1,"",2.2,0.0],[28,1,"",2.2,0.0],[29,1,"",2.147,0.0],[30,1,"",2.147,0.0],[31,1,"",2.08,0.0],